step_id": 2, "sub_question": "Which of [entity from step 1] was the longest lasting without being the grandest?", "goal": "Collect information for: Which of [entity from step 1] was the longest lasting without being the grandest?", "dependencies": [1], "expected_info_type": "general"}]}}, "reasoning_process": "Decomposing complex question into sub-questions", "retrieval_info": null, "success": true}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-19T22:04:26.040839", "agent_role": "Analysis-Answer", "input_data": {"sub_question": "List of amusement parks in Coney Island, Brooklyn, New York City", "num_documents": 4}, "output_data": {"raw_response": "{\n  \"status\": \"yes\",\n  \"answer\": \"The amusement parks in Coney Island, Brooklyn, New York City include: 1. Steeplechase Park (1897-1964, longest-lasting park), 2. Dreamland (1904-1911, burned in 1911), 3. Luna Park (original 1903-1944, later rebuilt as Luna Park 2010), and 4. Astroland Park (operated the Coney Island Cyclone roller coaster until 2008).\",\n  \"analysis\": \"The documents explicitly mention Steeplechase Park, Dreamland, and Luna Park as the three original iconic parks. They also reference Astroland Park (which operated the Cyclone) and the newer Luna Park (2010) at the former Astroland site. These constitute all the listed amusement parks in the area, with sufficient details about their operational history and locations.\"\n}", "parsed_result": {"status": "yes", "answer": "The amusement parks in Coney Island, Brooklyn, New York City include: 1. Steeplechase Park (1897-1964, longest-lasting park), 2. Dreamland (1904-1911, burned in 1911), 3. Luna Park (original 1903-1944, later rebuilt as Luna Park 2010), and 4. Astroland Park (operated the Coney Island Cyclone roller coaster until 2008).", "analysis": "The documents explicitly mention Steeplechase Park, Dreamland, and Luna Park as the three original iconic parks. They also reference Astroland Park (which operated the Cyclone) and the newer Luna Park (2010) at the former