ns", "retrieval_info": null, "success": true}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-19T23:44:04.276542", "agent_role": "Analysis-Answer", "input_data": {"sub_question": "Who is \u015aivar\u0101ma Swami?", "num_documents": 4}, "output_data": {"raw_response": "{\n  \"status\": \"yes\",\n  \"answer\": \"\u015aivar\u0101ma Swami (born 30 March 1949, Budapest, Hungary) is a Vaishnava guru and religious leader for the International Society for Krishna Consciousness (ISKCON). He serves on ISKCON's Governing Body Commission, leading the organization's mission in Hungary, Romania, and Turkey. Known for his expertise in Vaishnava literature, he has authored several books on Gaudiya Vaishnavism and conducts courses at Bhaktivedanta Manor on Gaudiya Vaishnava theology, including commentaries on the Venu Gita.\",\n  \"analysis\": \"The documents explicitly mention \u015aivar\u0101ma Swami's role in ISKCON, his responsibilities in the Governing Body Commission, his scholarly contributions to Vaishnava theology, and his teaching activities. The name is consistently spelled as 'Sivarama Swami' in the texts, which matches the query's variant spelling (\u015aivar\u0101ma Swami). This provides sufficient information to answer the question.\"\n}", "parsed_result": {"status": "yes", "answer": "\u015aivar\u0101ma Swami (born 30 March 1949, Budapest, Hungary) is a Vaishnava guru and religious leader for the International Society for Krishna Consciousness (ISKCON). He serves on ISKCON's Governing Body Commission, leading the organization's mission in Hungary, Romania, and Turkey. Known for his expertise in Vaishnava literature, he has authored several books on Gaudiya Vaishnavism and conducts courses at Bhaktivedanta Manor on Gaudiya Vaishnava theology, including commentaries on the Venu Gita.", "analysis": "The documents explicitly mention \u015aivar\u0101ma Swami's role in ISKCON, his responsibilities in the Governing Body Commission, his scholarly contributions to Vaishnava theology, and his teaching